# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.pyd
build/
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Data & heavy binaries (intentionally excluded from the public showcase)
*.pkl
*.parquet
*.h5
*.log
# ANCHORED TO THE ROOT.  Unanchored, `Data/` matches at ANY depth -- and on a
# case-insensitive filesystem it also swallowed `docs/data/`, which is where the
# published JSON lives.  The site would have deployed as a blank page saying it
# could not load its own data, with nothing in git status to explain why.
/Data/
_cache/
_*_cache/

# DERIVED, and vendor-priced.  All of these are rebuildable from the private
# panel, and all carry open/close data that must not reach a public repo -- see
# Live/README.md.  Ignored rather than trusted to discipline: 191 of the .npz
# fixtures below were staged by a stray `git add .` and caught only by chance.
#
# .cache/ holds the worksheet cache: one parquet per instrument plus a .key
# sidecar.  *.parquet was already covered, the .key files were not, and a
# directory rule is the honest way to say "none of this belongs in git".
# Rebuilt in ~290s by `trading_book.py --clear-cache` followed by a normal run.
#
# FX/*.csv is derived on the same terms and by the same script -- one file per
# conversion rate, rebuilt in seconds from the cached worksheets, carrying rates
# extrapolated from closes, which is the same class of data as the panel itself.
# The journal beside them is prose and IS tracked.
Live/2_Engine/Trading_book/
Live/2_Engine/FX/*.csv
# Stage 3's positions are derived from the books on the same terms, and
# rebuild in seconds.  portfolio.py and the journal are tracked.
Live/2_Engine/IRX/IRX.csv
Live/3_Portfolio/Positions/
Live/3_Portfolio/Portfolio.csv
# Stage 4's order ledger is derived from stage 3's positions on the same terms
# and rebuilds in ~1s.  It carries contract-level sizes for every session since
# 1990, which is the position book stated a second way -- if Positions/ does not
# belong in a public repo then neither does this.  bookkeeping.py is tracked.
Live/4_Bookkeeping/*.csv
# The journal STORE is data, and the most sensitive kind: every row carries a
# position, a price and the signal that produced it.  journal.py is tracked; the
# store never is.  A live store must also never be reconstructable from a public
# repo -- that is the whole point of it being append-only and local.
Live/4_Bookkeeping/Journal/orders/
Live/4_Bookkeeping/Journal/fills/
Live/4_Bookkeeping/Journal/MANIFEST.json
Live/4_Bookkeeping/Journal/_checksums.jsonl
# docs/ IS THE ONE PLACE VENDOR-DERIVED NUMBERS ARE PUBLISHED ON PURPOSE, and
# it is NOT ignored.  2026 only, open/close only, non-commercial -- the carve-out
# is stated in full in Live/README.md.  What lands there is written by
# Live/5_Publish/publish.py through a whitelist, never by hand: if you find
# yourself copying a file into docs/data/, stop, because the whitelist is the
# only thing standing between this repo and a licence problem.
.cache/
_reference_backup_*/

# Virtualenv -- created locally, never committed. See production/README.md.
.venv/
venv/

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# LaTeX build artefacts
*.aux
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk

# Stage 6 reads this for the site's "Updated" line; it is a local run
# artifact and reaches the repo through docs/data/latest.json.
Live/.pipeline_run.json

# front_contract.py regenerates this, and it carries vendor prices.
Live/1_Roll/Front_Contract/worksheet.csv

# Scheduled-run logs and status markers. Local only.
Live/logs/

# Local convenience launcher and its build artefacts.
Live/Run pipeline.exe
build/
dist/
*.spec
